"""How much scrim each painting needs — GENERATED by scripts/tune_art_scrim.py.

The scrim's SHAPE is shared and lives in `covers.scrim_alpha`: three bands
following the byline, the title and the mark, which sit in the same place on
every cover. How much of it a picture needs is a property of the picture, and
the span here is 0.30x to 1.00x — so one strength for all of
them has to be the maximum, and every other painting pays for the palest.

Measured, not chosen: each value is the least strength at which white type
still clears AA where it falls, found by walking upward.
`CoverAssetTests.test_every_painting_still_carries_white_type` re-measures
every entry against the artwork on disk, so a recropped painting fails the
build by name rather than shipping illegible.

`frontend/src/lib/coverScrim.ts` is the same table for the two renderers
that draw a cover; `coverScrim.test.ts` fails if the two drift.
"""

